In this lesson we'll look at finding a percentage of a quantity. The big idea is super simple: a percentage is just a fraction with one hundred on the bottom, so forty-five percent literally means forty-five out of one hundred. That means you can turn any percentage into a decimal by dividing by one hundred, or into a fraction by writing it over one hundred. Once you've done that, you just multiply by the quantity you're working with, and then round sensibly — to the nearest cent for money, or to whole units for things you can count. Here's a handy mental shortcut. Ten percent of any number is that number divided by ten. From there you can build almost anything: one percent is your ten percent divided by ten, five percent is your ten percent halved, twenty percent is double ten, twenty-five percent is the number divided by four, and fifty percent is just half. Finally, if you ever need to express one quantity as a percentage of another, set up a fraction with the whole on the bottom, then multiply by one hundred. And remember, the whole changes with the question, so always check which number is the whole first. Now let's see it in action.